He walked back   wider, more careful, giving the wardrobe a berth so dramatic he practically hugged the opposite wall. Each step still trembled through the floor. Each stride still ate enormous distance. But he watched the space around his shoulders now, turning slightly to clear obstacles, adjusting his trajectory with the self-conscious precision of someone driving a truck through a parking garage designed for sedans.

He reached the start. Turned. Walked the full pathway without collision. The wireframe went green. His gait was mechanical, deliberate, nothing like Ava's fluid grace   but it was functional. Shoulder-led. Wide-striding. The chrome rumbling in deep rhythm with each heel-strike. When he reached me at the end, he stopped   and the sudden halt sent no sway, no bounce, no cascade of shifting weight. His body just stopped. Planted. Immovable. Like dropping an anchor.

<<system "Gait pattern accepted. Both users demonstrate functional ambulation in their current avatars.">>

