<<system "Running demonstration. Both users will observe holographic models first. Do not attempt to run until instructed.">>

Two holographic figures materialized on the pathway   one Leona's build, one Avan's. Translucent blue. They stood at the start position, poised.

<<system "User Leona Hart. Running impact dynamics.">>

The holographic Leona began to run. Not fast   a moderate jog and the physics engine displayed everything. Every bounce, every sway, every chain reaction of kinetic force   mapped in glowing vectors and annotated with clinical labels.

Her breasts moved first. The initial stride produced a forward lurch, and the chest tissue   unsupported, uncompressed   followed a visible oscillation pattern. Up on impact. Forward on momentum. Down on gravity. The system drew the trajectory: a figure-eight pattern, each breast moving semi-independently, the combined motion producing up to 15 centimeters of vertical displacement per stride. Red warning markers appeared at the Cooper's ligaments   the internal support structures   flagged with strain indicators.

<<system "Unsupported running in this avatar produces significant chest tissue displacement. Vertical oscillation exceeds safe parameters for sustained activity. Impact forces transmit through the breast tissue to the ligament network, causing discomfort ranging from moderate to severe depending on duration and intensity.">>

The holographic model's butt was next   the round, heavy mass responding to each foot-strike with a visible ripple of movement. Gluteal bounce. Thigh oscillation   the inner thighs compressing and releasing with every stride, soft tissue in contact creating friction and heat. Even the hair   the long waves streaming behind the running figure   produced drag and lateral sway that affected head position and neck strain.

Everything moved. Everything. In waves and ripples and cascading chains of soft-tissue momentum that turned the simple act of running into a full-body physics event.

