I stared at the holographic model. At the annotated figure-eights. At the red strain markers. At the 15-centimeter bounce measurement and I thought about every time I'd gone for a run   light, easy, nothing on my chest but a t-shirt, nothing bouncing, nothing swaying, nothing hurting   and the gulf between that memory and this reality opened beneath me like a canyon.

<<system "User Avan Morgan. Running impact dynamics.">>

The holographic Avan began to run. The contrast was immediate and violent. Where the Leona model was all cascading wave-motion, the Avan model was a battering ram. Minimal bounce   the low body-fat percentage and dense musculature eliminated almost all soft-tissue oscillation. The momentum was linear, direct, devastating. Each stride covered enormous distance. The legs drove like pistons   quads firing, hamstrings pulling, calves launching. The ground-reaction force markers at each foot-strike showed numbers that would crack pavement.

<<system "This avatar's running dynamics are momentum-dominant. Minimal tissue displacement. Maximum force transfer. Ground-reaction forces at full sprint exceed four times body weight   approximately 750 kilograms of force per foot-strike.">>

Avan's eyes widened.

<<system "However.">>

