<<system "External genitalia are vulnerable during high-impact movement. Testicular tissue is suspended in the scrotal sac with limited structural support. Running, jumping, sudden directional changes, or impact to the groin region produces oscillation and compression of testicular tissue that ranges from mildly uncomfortable to acutely painful.">>

The holographic model demonstrated. A subtle   but clearly visible   movement pattern in the groin area. The testes responding to each stride's impact with their own small, pendulous bounce. Strain markers appeared at the spermatic cord attachment points. The system drew a vector showing how a sudden change in direction   a lateral dodge, a sharp stop   could whip the unsupported tissue sideways against the inner thigh.

