The holographic model took a simulated impact to the groin. A knee-height obstacle clipping the inner thigh and deflecting upward. The model crumpled   folding at the waist, hands dropping to the affected area, knees buckling inward. The pain indicators lit up in screaming red across the entire pelvic region, the lower abdomen, and   inexplicably   the stomach.

<<system "Direct impact to the testicles produces a pain response that radiates through the spermatic plexus into the abdominal cavity. This is widely considered one of the most acute pain responses in male anatomy. Unlike most pain, it is accompanied by nausea, diaphragmatic spasm, and temporary loss of motor function. The instinct to protect the groin is not learned   it will develop rapidly as your body maps this vulnerability.">>

Avan's hands had already moved. Subtle. Unconscious. Drifting downward, hovering in front of his hips, fingers slightly cupped. The protective instinct arriving in real time, written into the hardware before the software had finished processing. His face was pale beneath the bronze   a specific, focused horror that I recognized from every locker-room story I'd ever heard, except now it was Ava wearing that expression on a face carved from myth.

<<avan "I need… I need the supportive garments. Now.">>

<<system "Garment fitting will be addressed in Module 9. For now, be aware of the vulnerability. Move accordingly.">>

<<system "Both users may now attempt a brief running demonstration. Three strides only. The pathway is marked.">>

Three amber markers appeared   spaced evenly along the pathway. Start. Midpoint. Stop.

I went first. Set my feet. Took a breath. Pushed off.

The first stride was wrong   too long, too hard, Leo's running instinct slamming through my legs   and the impact that traveled up through my body hit my chest like a seismic wave. Both breasts lurched upward with the force, hung at the apex for a sickening instant, then crashed back down. The weight pulled my shoulders forward. My spine curved. My second stride shortened automatically   my body learning during the motion that shorter meant less impact meant less pain   and by the third stride I was running in quick, compact steps, arms pressed close to my torso, chest still bouncing but with diminishing amplitude as the shorter stride reduced the ground-force.

I stopped at the third marker. Breathing hard. One arm had crossed over my chest   pressing my breasts inward, compressing the tissue against my ribcage. The relief was immediate. The system had not told me to do that. My body had done it on its own.

<<system "Noted. User Leona Hart demonstrates instinctive self-support behavior. The adaptation is correct. This reflex will strengthen.">>

Avan took his position. Set wide. The chrome trembled beneath him as he shifted weight to his lead foot.

He launched.

The first stride cracked the air. The raw, explosive power that detonated through his legs sent him hurtling forward with a force that was   terrifying. He crossed the first marker before I'd fully registered his start. The chrome screamed beneath each impact. His arms pumped in massive arcs, shoulders rolling like turbines, the momentum building with each stride into something that looked less like running and more like a directed avalanche.

He hit the third marker and tried to stop. Planted his lead foot. The quadricep fired   all that coiled, oversized muscle clenching at once   and the deceleration slammed through his frame like hitting a wall. His body pitched forward. Arms windmilling. He staggered   one step, two   chest heaving, sweat breaking fresh across his brow   and stopped.

Three strides had covered the distance that took me seven in walking pace.

He stood there. Chest pounding. Eyes wide. Looking down at legs that had just performed something his mind couldn't reconcile with anything Ava Morgan had ever asked her body to do.

<<avan "That was… three STEPS?">>

<<system "Your avatar generates approximately 4.2 times the locomotor force of your original body. Calibrate accordingly. Uncontrolled acceleration risks collision, environmental damage, and injury to others.">>

He looked at his legs. At the thighs thick as tree trunks, still trembling with residual force. At the chrome floor where his heel-strikes had left three faint scuff marks in a line. Then he looked at me   small, flushed, one arm still hugging my chest, standing at the other end of the runway in a body that made running feel like trying to sprint while carrying a shelf of unsecured cargo.

Something moved across his face. Not amusement. Not pity. Something more complicated. The recognition that we were experiencing the same redesign from opposite ends of the same spectrum   him with too much power and no idea how to contain it, me with too much softness and no idea how to move through it.

<<system "Module 3 complete. Walking and running fundamentals acquired. Both users demonstrate functional mobility within acceptable desync-prevention parameters.">>

The amber pathway dimmed. The mirrors relaxed to passive reflection. The holographic impact diagrams dissolved into motes of light that the floor's pulse-veins drank in.

<<system "Module 4 will begin in ninety seconds. Subject: Sitting and Positional Awareness. Use this interval to practice walking independently.">>

Avan walked toward me. Slowly this time. Shoulder-led, wide-striding, each step controlled and measured   giving the wardrobe eight feet of clearance. When he reached me he stopped and looked down from his full height, and his expression was the complicated, exhausted tenderness of someone who had just learned that his legs were weapons and his girlfriend's boyfriend's body was a physics problem.

<<avan "You okay?">>

<<leona "My chest hurts.">>

<<avan "My everything hurts.">>

We stood there. Two functional walkers. Two terrible runners. Two people learning the mechanics of flesh they hadn't ordered, in a room that measured every heartbeat and painted it in neon on the walls.

Ninety seconds. The city glowed. Module 4 was coming.

Somewhere beneath the ache in my unsupported chest and the burn in my overtaxed hips, a very small, very quiet part of me registered something strange: three strides in   just before the bouncing became unbearable   the feeling of my body moving in its corrected gait had been fluid. Rolling. Almost... graceful.

I buried the thought immediately. Pressed it flat. Locked it in a box.

The mirrors didn't catch it. The neon didn't read it. Some things stayed private, even in a room that saw everything.

[[Familiarization Module 4 Starting|day_5_17_str]]

:: day_5_17_str

<<system "Module 4: Sitting and Positional Awareness. Initiating.">>

The apartment shifted.

Furniture materialized from the floor   rising through the chrome like objects surfacing from black water. A straight-backed chair, sleek and minimal, its seat a hard polished composite. The edge of the hovering bed   still draped in those holographic sheets that rippled through violet and rose-gold. A low floor cushion   circular, thick, a deep plum-colored pad that settled onto the chrome with a soft exhale of compressed air and a low couch   curved, backless, upholstered in something dark and faintly luminous, barely thirty centimeters off the ground.

Four surfaces. Four different heights. Four different problems.

The holographic mirrors angled inward once more   tracking, always tracking   and the wireframe overlays reactivated. Faint blue skeletons waiting to be superimposed over our reflections the moment we sat.

<<system "Sitting is not a passive act. In a body that differs from your cognitive model, seated positions produce unexpected sensory feedback, balance challenges, and physical discomfort if approached incorrectly. Both users will practice sitting on each provided surface.">>

<<system "User Leona Hart. Begin with the chair.">>

The chair. Hard-surfaced. Straight-backed. The kind of utilitarian seat Leo had dropped into ten thousand times without a single thought   just collapse, sprawl, done.

I approached it. Turned. Started to sit the way I'd always sat   weight falling straight down, legs apart, spine loose, a controlled drop onto the seat.

The moment my body made contact, everything was wrong.

My hips were wider than the chair's seat. Not by much   but enough that instead of settling into the chair, my sit bones landed on the edges, the broader pelvic structure spanning the surface in a way that distributed my weight differently than I'd ever experienced. My thighs, thicker and softer than Leo's, pressed together as my knees defaulted inward   not by choice but by the femoral angle the system had drilled into me during Module 2 and between those pressed thighs, in the compressed space where soft tissue met hard surface 

I felt everything.

The contact was immediate and startling. Warm pressure   my vulva pressing against the chair's surface through the thin synth-fabric, weight settling directly onto tissue that was packed with nerve endings I hadn't possessed an hour ago. The hard seat offered no give. No cushion. Just flat, unyielding composite pushing up against anatomy that registered the pressure with a clarity that made my breath hitch.

<<leona "Oh ">>

It wasn't pain. It wasn't pleasure. It was   awareness. Sudden, inescapable awareness of a part of my body that made contact with the world in a way that Leo's body never had. When Leo sat, the contact points were bones and muscle   sit bones, glutes, thighs. Hard structure meeting hard surface. Nothing between them that felt things independently.

This was different. This was soft tissue compressed against hard surface, warmth building where pressure concentrated, nerve endings firing in a low, persistent hum that spread from the point of contact up through my pelvis and into my lower abdomen.

I shifted. Tried to adjust. The movement dragged fabric across the compressed tissue and the friction produced a small, bright spark of sensation that raced through me like a current. I froze.

<<system "You are experiencing genital contact pressure. In this avatar, seated positions place the vulva in direct contact with the sitting surface. Unlike male anatomy   which rests primarily above the surface   female anatomy compresses against it. The sensation is normal and will vary based on surface hardness, fabric thickness, and seated duration.">>

<<leona "It's… I can feel the CHAIR.">>

<<system "Correct. Hard surfaces concentrate pressure on the perineum and clitoral region. Softer surfaces distribute it more broadly. Sitting posture also affects pressure distribution   crossing your legs, tilting your pelvis, or shifting your weight will alter which structures bear the most contact.">>

The system paused. Then continued with the same flat, clinical detachment it had maintained throughout   but the information it delivered hit like a slap.

<<system "Note: certain seated positions create sustained pressure on the clitoris. This may produce involuntary physiological arousal   increased blood flow, lubrication response, heightened sensitivity   without conscious sexual intent. This is a mechanical response to pressure stimulation. It is not a malfunction. It does not indicate desire. It is anatomy responding to physics.">>

My face went nuclear. The pulse-veins in every wall within three meters erupted in rose-neon   screaming pink   broadcasting my mortification across the apartment in high-definition bioluminescent shame. My thighs clenched together tighter, which only increased the pressure, which only increased the awareness, which only deepened the blush, which only brightened the walls.

<<leona "Can we   can we MOVE ON ">>

<<system "Not yet. Cross your legs.">>

I stared at the mirror. At the wireframe waiting patiently over my reflection. Crossed my legs.

The motion was   complicated. My thighs pressed together with a soft, heavy compression that Leo's lean legs had never produced. The upper thigh settled over the lower one, and the weight of it   the genuine mass of my thighs   created a seal of warm skin against warm skin that I could feel from hip to knee. My hips tilted slightly with the cross, shifting my pelvis, and the pressure pattern on the chair changed entirely. The direct contact eased   replaced by a different kind of compression, thigh-to-thigh, that trapped warmth between my legs in a way that was less acute but more pervasive.

My breasts shifted. The cross-legged posture tilted my torso slightly, and the heavy tissue on my chest responded   settling to one side, the left breast resting partially atop the right, their combined weight pulling at the skin between them. The change in chest position altered my breathing   each inhale pressed the compressed tissue harder together, and each exhale allowed them to separate with a soft shift that I could feel against the sensitive undersides.

<<system "Cross-legged sitting reduces direct vulvar contact but increases inner thigh compression and lateral breast displacement. The warmth buildup between your thighs is due to the increased subcutaneous fat layer and reduced airflow. This body retains heat in contact zones more readily than your original body.">>

I uncrossed. Crossed the other way. Different pressure. Different weight distribution. The same impossible, inescapable awareness that every seated position in this body was a negotiation between bone structure, soft tissue, and nerve endings that I couldn't switch off.

<<system "Now. The floor cushion.">>

I stood   and the act of standing from the hard chair required a muscle engagement pattern that threw me. Leo would have pushed up with his arms, leveraged his back, risen from the shoulders. But my upper body strength was halved, my arms were thinner, and my center of gravity sat in my pelvis. The push from my arms barely moved me. I had to engage my glutes   clench and drive upward from the hips   and the motion felt like squatting in reverse, my thighs and butt doing the actual work of lifting while my upper body just went along for the ride.

The floor cushion was better. Significantly better. I sank onto it   legs folding beneath me in a kneeling position   and the plush surface distributed the pressure across a wide area. No sharp compression. No focused contact point. The softness absorbed my weight and cradled the tissue between my legs rather than pushing into it. I actually exhaled   real relief, tension draining from muscles I hadn't realized were clenched.

<<system "Softer surfaces distribute genital pressure more evenly and reduce point-contact stimulation. Note the difference in comfort between the hard chair and the cushion. When possible, this avatar benefits from softer seating.">>

The bed edge was somewhere between   firm enough to press, soft enough to give. The holographic sheets rippled against my bare thighs as I sat, their temperature-responsive surface warming instantly to my skin. The low couch was the trickiest   thirty centimeters off the ground meant lowering myself nearly to the floor, which required me to hinge at the hips and control the descent entirely with my legs. Going down was manageable. Getting back up was a struggle that ended with me using the couch arm as a lever and my glutes screaming.

<<system "Rising from low surfaces in this avatar requires posterior chain dominance   gluteal and quadricep engagement. Your upper body cannot generate sufficient force to push you upright. Always lead with your hips. Always drive from below.">>

<<system "User Avan Morgan. Begin with the chair.">>

[[Continue Module 4|day_5_17_str_1]]

:: day_5_17_str_1

Avan approached. He'd been watching   arms crossed, jaw tight, the complicated expression of someone who'd just watched another person discover an entirely alien sensory world and knew their own version was coming.

He turned. Sat.

Fast. The way Ava sat   a quick, efficient drop, knees together, hands in lap. Compact. Neat. Feminine.

His full weight hit the chair in a single, unbraced impact. 188 pounds of dense muscle and bone crashing onto hard composite with legs pressed tight together.

His testicles   suspended in their vulnerable sac between his thighs   caught the full force of the compression.

The sound Avan made was not a word. It was a guttural, airless, visceral noise   torn from somewhere below his diaphragm, a frequency of pain that his deep voice transformed into something almost subsonic. His mouth opened but nothing else came out. His body folded   curling forward at the waist, shoulders hunching, hands shooting between his legs   and for three full seconds he was perfectly, completely still, bent double on the chair, every muscle in his massive frame locked in a full-body cramp of agony.

<<avan "Hhhkk ">>

Then the nausea hit. I could see it   the color draining from his bronze face, the sweat breaking instantly across his brow, the involuntary shudder that rippled through his torso. The neon veins in the wall behind him went haywire   spiking white, red, white, red   reading a pain response so acute the system's biometric displays flickered.

<<system "User Avan Morgan has experienced testicular compression trauma. This is the result of sitting with legs closed and without pre-positioning external genitalia.">>

<<avan "I   I'm going to   oh GOD ">>

He rocked forward. Hands still buried between his thighs, forehead nearly touching his knees, breathing in short, sharp gasps that shook his broad shoulders. The pain was radiating   I could see it in the way his abdominal muscles clenched in waves, the way his thighs trembled, the way his eyes squeezed shut so hard the tendons in his neck stood like cables.

<<leona "Ava! Ava   are you okay ">>

I was beside him before I thought about it   my hand on his enormous shoulder, fingers tiny against the rolling mass of muscle. His skin was hot. Damp. Trembling.

<<avan "It's   it HURTS   it's in my STOMACH   why is it in my stomach ">>

<<system "Testicular pain radiates through the spermatic plexus into the abdominal cavity. The nausea is a vagal nerve response. Both will subside within 30 to 90 seconds. Do not attempt to stand. Breathe slowly.">>

He breathed. Ragged. Wet. Each exhale a shudder that I could feel through my palm on his shoulder. The wall-veins slowly dimmed from their panic-red back toward blue   his heart rate dropping from critical to merely terrible. After a full minute he straightened. Slowly. His face was grey beneath the bronze, and his eyes   when he opened them   were glassy with tears that hadn't fallen.

<<avan "Nobody… told me… that was there.">>

<<system "It is being told to you now. External genitalia must be positioned before sitting. Every time. Without exception.">>

The wireframe overlay activated on his reflection. A correction diagram appeared   not a posture guide this time but a seating preparation sequence. Step one: approach the seat. Step two: before lowering, use one hand to adjust the penis and testicles to one side   typically the left or right thigh, depending on comfort. Step three: lower slowly, knees apart, allowing the adjusted tissue to rest against the inner thigh rather than compressing beneath body weight. Step four: settle weight gradually. Never drop.

<<system "The adjustment should become reflexive. With practice, it takes less than one second and is not visible to observers. For now, perform it consciously.">>

Avan stood. Carefully. Like a man made of bruised glass. He approached the chair again. Stopped. His face flushed dark   and for the first time since the transformation, I saw Ava's embarrassment flooding through Avan's features. Not the panic-embarrassment of being trapped in the wrong body. The specific, human embarrassment of being told to touch yourself in a clinical setting while someone watches.

His hand moved. Quick, deliberately casual   a downward brush along his left thigh that repositioned the tissue through the thin fabric. Then he sat. Slowly. Knees apart   wider than Ava had ever sat in her life, the "male sit" that the system demanded. His weight settled gradually, distributed across his broader sit bones, the gap between his thighs leaving space for the adjusted anatomy.

No pain. His face showed naked relief.

<<system "Correct. Note the knee position   wider than your instinct suggests. This avatar requires clearance between the thighs at all times when seated. Crossing legs tightly   as your original body did   will compress the testicles against the inner thigh and produce the pain response you just experienced.">>

<<avan "So I just   I can never cross my legs again?">>

<<system "You may cross at the ankle. You may rest one ankle on the opposite knee   the 'figure four' position   which provides an open geometry that avoids genital compression. Traditional knee-over-knee crossing is possible only if the tissue is first adjusted and the cross is kept loose. Tight compression will always produce pain.">>

Avan tried the ankle cross. Workable. The figure-four   one massive ankle resting on the opposite knee, thighs forming a wide diamond. The position looked natural on his frame   broad, open, commanding   and kept the vulnerable tissue completely uncompressed. He exhaled.

<<avan "That's   okay. That works.">>

<<system "Hard surfaces.">>

Avan looked at the chair beneath him. Shifted. The hard composite offered no cushioning   and now that the acute pain had faded, he registered what I'd registered on the same surface: the specific, unpadded contact of sensitive tissue against an unforgiving seat. Not crushing. Not agonizing. But present. A low, persistent awareness of pressure on structures that hung freely when standing and suddenly bore weight when seated.

<<system "Hard surfaces provide no absorption for scrotal tissue. Prolonged sitting on hard surfaces produces a gradual ache that builds over time   discomfort in the perineum, warmth in the groin, restlessness. This is why male-bodied individuals frequently shift position while seated.">>

<<avan "So THAT'S why boys can never sit still.">>

The observation came out before she could filter it   Ava's voice, Ava's thought, delivered in Avan's bass   and the contrast was so unexpectedly human that something cracked in the room's tension. Not laughter. Not relief. Just a breath. A flicker. The wall-veins caught the shift in both our heart rates   a tiny synchronous dip   and softened to warm violet for a single pulse before returning to clinical blue-white.

<<system "The observation is physiologically accurate. Seated restlessness in male anatomy is partially driven by the need to periodically reposition external genitalia for comfort. This reflex will develop.">>

The remaining surfaces followed. The floor cushion was better   Avan knelt in a wide position, thighs apart, the plush surface cradling rather than compressing. The bed edge was manageable   soft enough to absorb impact, firm enough to support his enormous weight. The low couch was his worst enemy   lowering 188 pounds to thirty centimeters required leg strength he had in abundance but coordination he lacked, and his first attempt ended with him dropping the last ten centimeters with a jarring impact that made him wince and immediately adjust.

<<system "Always control the final descent. Even on soft surfaces, impact compresses tissue. Lower   do not drop.">>

By the end of the surface rotation, Avan had developed a visible pre-sitting ritual: approach, adjust, lower slowly, settle wide. The movements were still conscious and self-aware   but the architecture of the habit was forming. His hand moving down to reposition before each seat. His knees spreading before his weight committed. His descent controlled and measured.

<<system "Module 4 complete. Both users demonstrate functional seated awareness within acceptable desync-prevention parameters.">>

The extra furniture sank back into the chrome floor   descending as smoothly as it had risen   leaving only the hovering bed and the curved couch as permanent fixtures. The mirrors relaxed. The wireframes dissolved.

<<system "Module 5 will begin in ninety seconds. Subject: Upper Body Familiarization. Use this interval to practice seated-to-standing transitions.">>

I sat on the bed edge. Sank into the holographic sheets   their warmth blooming against my thighs and the undersides of my legs, the soft surface distributing pressure into something almost comfortable. Almost bearable. The persistent hum of contact between my legs was still there   I was starting to think it would always be there, in every seat, on every surface   but the bed's give muffled it into background noise rather than foreground alarm.

Avan lowered himself beside me. Slowly. Adjusted. Sat wide. The bed groaned under his weight   the hovering frame dipping slightly, compensating   and the holographic sheets rippled outward from where he settled, violet wavelets spreading across the surface like ripples in a chrome pond.

We sat side by side. A small woman and a large man on the edge of a floating bed. Our reflections stared back from the dark windows   Eidolon City blazing behind them, neon rain catching light, hover lanes streaming fire. Two silhouettes that could have been any couple in the world, sitting close, saying nothing.

Except we weren't any couple. We were reversed. Inverted. Two minds in wrong-direction bodies learning that even the simplest act of sitting down was a negotiation with anatomy that didn't match the person inside.

Avan's hand found the space between us on the mattress. Rested there. Open.

I put my hand in it. Small against large. My fingers disappeared into his palm.

Neither of us spoke. The neon veins wove our heartbeats together in the walls   Leona's fast and humming, Avan's deep and steady   and the city glowed, and the bed held us, and for ninety seconds there was no module, no guide, no system voice.

Just two people sitting. Badly. In new bodies. Together.

[[Familiarization Module 5 Starting|day_5_18_str]]


:: day_5_18_str

<<system "Module 5: Upper Body Familiarization. Initiating.">>

The mirrors tightened. The 360-degree arc contracted   panels gliding inward on invisible tracks until they formed a closer ring, a more intimate cage of reflection. The angle shifted too   tilting slightly downward, optimizing for torso-level display rather than full-body. The system wanted us to see our upper halves. Nothing else. Nowhere to hide.

Neon overlays materialized on our reflections. Not the skeletal wireframes from earlier   these were softer, more detailed. Topographic sensitivity maps drawn in shifting color gradients. Heat maps of nerve density laid directly onto our mirrored skin like luminous tattoos.

Mine was a landscape of fire.

The overlay painted my chest in graduated layers of color   cool blue at the outer edges of the breast tissue, warming through green to amber across the upper curves, deepening to hot orange along the heavy undersides where the tissue hung fullest. The areolae blazed red. The nipples   small, pert points that the thin synth-fabric did nothing to conceal   burned white-hot. Maximum density. Maximum sensitivity. Two incandescent points on a topographic map of tactile vulnerability.

<<system "User Leona Hart. Upper body familiarization begins with primary secondary sexual characteristics: breast tissue.">>

I stared at the overlay. At the gradients of color draped across a chest I'd had for less than two hours. The system continued without waiting for acknowledgment.

<<system "Your avatar's breasts are classified as full DD-cup, high-profile, with natural teardrop-to-round projection. Combined mass: approximately 1.2 kilograms. Each breast is a complex structure of glandular tissue, adipose fat, Cooper's ligaments, and a vascular network that responds to temperature, hormonal state, and direct stimulation.">>

Clinical. Flat. As if it were describing a mechanical component. But the words landed on me like weights   1.2 kilograms hanging from my chest, permanently, in a structure that responds to everything.

<<system "You must understand the weight. Cup your breasts from below. Lift and release.">>

I didn't move.

<<system "This exercise is mandatory. Failure to complete tactile calibration increases Stage 1 desync probability by 28%. You must develop a conscious sensory relationship with your avatar's anatomy to prevent cognitive rejection.">>

I looked at Avan. He was staring at a point on the wall six inches above my head, deliberately not watching, jaw clenched so tight I could see the muscle flexing. Giving me what privacy the room allowed. Which was none   the mirrors showed everything from every angle   but the intention mattered.

I raised my hands. Placed them beneath my breasts and lifted.

The sensation unfolded in layers. First   my palms. The skin of my hands meeting the skin of my chest through the vanishingly thin synth-fabric, and the contact registering on both sides simultaneously. My palms felt softness   yielding, heavy, warm tissue that compressed slightly under even gentle pressure. My chest felt hands   the pressure of fingers against the sensitive underside, each fingertip a distinct point of contact, mapped in the overlay's amber-to-orange zone where nerve density climbed steeply.

Then   the weight. The actual, physical, gravitational reality of what my body carried. My hands took the load and the difference was immediate. My shoulders relaxed. My lower back unclenched. Muscles I hadn't realized were working suddenly stopped working because my hands were doing their job. 1.2 kilograms didn't sound like much   until you'd been carrying it unsupported on the front of your ribcage, cantilevered, shifting with every breath, pulling at your spine with every step.

<<system "Note the postural relief. Your chest muscles, back muscles, and shoulder girdle are under constant low-level strain compensating for breast weight. This fatigue accumulates over time without support.">>

Then   the release. The system had said lift and release. I opened my hands. Withdrew them and the tissue fell.

Not far. Not dramatically. But the drop   from cupped support to freefall back to their natural hanging position   produced a bounce that cascaded through the entire structure. The heavy undersides swung downward, momentum carried the tissue past its resting point, elasticity pulled it back, and the oscillation repeated in diminishing waves. Three bounces. Maybe four. Each one sending a ripple of sensation through the nerve-dense tissue that started at the underside, swept upward across the full curve, crested at the areolae, and concentrated at the nipples with a sharpness that made my stomach clench.

<<leona "Nnh ">>

The sound escaped before I caught it. Small. Involuntary. The overlay on the mirror flared   the areolae zones pulsing from red to white and back   tracking the nerve response in real time. Broadcasting it. I crossed my arms over my chest instinctively and the compression produced its own cascade   tissue pressing inward, nipples dragging against the fabric of my arms, sensitivity spiking in a different configuration.

<<system "The sensitivity you are experiencing is baseline for this avatar. It is not heightened by the exercise   this is your body's normal response to direct tactile input. The nipples and areolae contain the highest concentration of nerve endings in your chest anatomy   comparable in density to the fingertips. Any contact   touch, pressure, fabric friction, temperature change   will register at this intensity.">>

Fabric friction. The words sank in. I was suddenly, acutely aware of the synth-fabric draped over my chest   the tissue-thin material that I'd barely noticed until now. It was touching my nipples. Had been touching them the entire time. A constant, low-frequency drag of woven material against the two most sensitive points on my torso. I'd filtered it as background noise. But now that the system had named it   now that I knew what was happening   the sensation surfaced from beneath my awareness like something rising from deep water, and suddenly I could feel every fiber. Every micro-movement of the fabric as I breathed. Every slight shift as my chest rose and fell.

<<leona "I can feel   the fabric   it's ">>

<<system "Correct. Unsupported breast tissue in motion produces constant fabric interaction at the nipple and areola. The sensation is persistent. A properly fitted bra eliminates the majority of this friction by encapsulating the tissue in a structured cup that moves with the breast rather than across it.">>

<<system "Bra mechanics will be covered in Module 9. For now, understand the principle: support reduces friction, limits oscillation, distributes weight, and decreases the sensory load your chest places on your nervous system. Without support, the sensory input from your breasts is constant and cumulative.">>

I wanted Module 9 to be next. I wanted it desperately. Anything to stop feeling every thread of this fabric against skin that could apparently detect individual fibers.

<<system "Temperature sensitivity demonstration.">>

<<leona "Wait   what ">>

The apartment's climate system activated. Not the warm, ambient currents from before   this was targeted. A single stream of cool air, directed from a vent I couldn't see, channeled precisely across my upper body.

The cold hit my collarbones first. Spread downward. Reached the upper curves of my chest and the skin prickled   goosebumps rising across the tissue like a wave racing toward shore. The synth-fabric offered no insulation. The cool air penetrated it as though it weren't there, and when it reached my nipples 

They hardened. Instantly. Visibly. The soft, relaxed tissue contracting into tight, prominent points that pressed against the fabric with a definition that left nothing to imagination. I felt it happen   felt the muscle behind each areola clench, felt the nipple itself draw inward and then push outward, felt the sensitivity spike as the contracted tissue concentrated every nerve ending into a smaller, denser, more exposed point.

The mirrors showed it all. From every angle. Every single mirror in the arc reflected two small, unmistakable peaks pushing through thin fabric. The overlay went incandescent   the nipple zones burning white against the darker gradient of the surrounding breast, the nerve-response data scrolling in clinical columns beside my reflection.

<<leona "STOP   turn it off   STOP THE COLD ">>

The cool air ceased. The climate system resumed neutral. But the damage was done   the contraction held, the nipples remaining tight and prominent even as the ambient temperature returned to normal. They would relax eventually. I knew that from biology, from health class, from a lifetime of understanding breasts as abstract concepts studied from the outside. But feeling it from the inside   feeling the contraction, the exposure, the involuntary broadcast of a physical response that I couldn't suppress or control   was something biology class had never prepared me for.

The walls were rose-pink again. Of course they were. The apartment had read my humiliation and was wearing it like wallpaper.

<<system "Temperature-induced nipple contraction is involuntary and visible through most fabrics. In social environments, this response may draw attention. Layered clothing or padded bra cups mitigate visibility. The response cannot be consciously suppressed.">>

I wrapped my arms around myself and said nothing. The overlays kept glowing. The mirrors kept reflecting. Somewhere inside the system's cold architecture, Module 5 continued without pausing for the small death occurring inside my chest.

<<system "Additional upper body parameters. Shoulder width: decreased 14% from original user. Reach envelope has narrowed laterally but improved vertically. Demonstrate: raise both arms overhead.">>

I lifted my arms. The motion was   easier. Surprisingly, noticeably easier. My narrower shoulders allowed a range of upward motion that felt freer, less obstructed. My hands rose above my head without the muscular resistance Leo's broader frame used to produce. But the motion also lifted my breasts   the tissue rising with the extension of my ribcage, the weight shifting upward momentarily   and when I lowered my arms, they settled back down with that same soft, heavy drop.

<<system "Now extend both arms laterally. Full wingspan.">>

I stretched sideways. Immediately felt the difference. My reach was shorter. Not dramatically   but enough to notice. The narrower shoulder structure meant my fingertips didn't extend as far. Where Leo could reach across a table, Leona would have to lean. Where Leo could span a doorframe, Leona fell inches short.

<<system "Grip strength has decreased approximately 50%. Demonstrate: squeeze your right hand into a fist as tightly as possible.">>

I squeezed. My forearm muscles clenched   thin, lean, the tendons visible under smooth skin   and the fist I produced was tight but small. I could feel the difference. The compression. The force my hand could generate meeting a ceiling that sat halfway between Leo's maximum and something that felt frustratingly inadequate. Opening a tight jar. Carrying a heavy bag. Gripping a railing on a sharp turn. All recalculated. All reduced.

<<system "This concludes the primary familiarization for User Leona Hart's upper body. Summary: your chest is a constant sensory input source that requires management through support garments and environmental awareness. Your upper body strength is significantly reduced. Your reach is narrower. Adjustment to these parameters is essential for desync prevention.">>

I dropped my arms. Hugged myself. Felt the weight settle against my forearms and tried not to think about the fact that I could feel each individual finger against the underside curve through the fabric.

<<system "User Avan Morgan. Upper body familiarization.">>

The overlays shifted. The fire map on my reflection dimmed as the system redirected its attention. New gradients painted across Avan's mirror image   and the difference was staggering.

Where my overlay had been a complex topography of sensitivity zones and nerve clusters, Avan's upper body was rendered in cool, even blue. Uniform. Stable. The chest   that massive, squared-off shelf of pectoral muscle   showed minimal nerve variation. Dense tissue. Low sensitivity. The overlay marked it as structural, not sensory. A wall, not a landscape.

<<system "User Avan Morgan. Your chest anatomy has undergone complete restructuring. Glandular breast tissue, adipose deposits, and Cooper's ligament networks have been entirely replaced by pectoral musculature. You carry no breast tissue.">>

[[Continue Module 4|day_5_18_str_1]]

:: day_5_18_str_1

Avan was still. The words hung in the air   clinical, factual, indifferent   and I watched something move through his expression that had nothing to do with the module. Nothing to do with the guide.

He raised his hand. Slowly. Pressed it flat against his chest   against the hard, unyielding surface of his left pectoral, fingers spread, palm testing the terrain.

Nothing gave. Nothing compressed. Nothing bounced or shifted or swayed. His fingers found only muscle   dense, layered, hard as packed earth beneath bronze skin. The overlay showed the contact registering as a dim blue glow. Minimal nerve response. Functional tactile awareness. No sensitivity spike. No involuntary reaction. No warmth shooting to his core.

His hand moved higher. To where the center of his chest met the sternum. Where   on Ava's body   the soft inner curves of two small B-cup breasts would have pressed together. Where she would have felt the familiar weight of herself. The gentle compression of lying on her stomach. The way a necklace pendant rested in the shallow valley between them.

Flat. Hard. A ridge of bone beneath a plate of muscle. Nothing there. Nothing.

His hand dropped. His reflection stared back   broad, powerful, magnificently male   and in the green eyes that still belonged to Ava Morgan, something crumbled. Not dramatically. Not with tears or sound. Just a quiet implosion behind the irises, like a candle guttering in a sealed room.

<<avan "They're gone.">>

Two words. Bass register. Barely audible. Not a discovery   he'd known since the transformation. But knowing and touching the place where they used to be were different things entirely. The first was information. The second was grief.

<<system "Correct. This avatar carries no breast tissue. Chest sensitivity is concentrated in the nipple and areola only, at significantly lower intensity than the female equivalent. Primary chest sensation is proprioceptive   awareness of muscle contraction, force output, and structural integrity.">>

The system did not pause for grief. The system did not recognize it. The overlay brightened and moved to shoulders.

<<system "Shoulder anatomy. Your shoulder girdle has expanded by 37%   your deltoids, trapezius, and rotator cuff complex are dramatically larger and more powerful. Demonstrate: extend both arms laterally.">>

Avan raised his arms. The span was enormous   fingertip to fingertip stretching wider than the mirror panel, forcing the system to zoom the reflection out. The deltoids   round, striated, capped on each shoulder like armored pauldrons   lifted the arms with an ease that visibly startled him. Where Ava would have felt the strain of holding her arms level for more than a few seconds, Avan's muscles bore the load as though it weren't there.

<<system "Now rotate your shoulders through their full range. Forward circle. Backward circle.">>

He rolled. Forward   the massive shoulders grinding through the rotation with a deep, mechanical smoothness, the pectoral plates shifting, the back muscles rippling in the mirror. Backward   the same rotation in reverse, but tighter. Noticeably tighter. The range narrowed.

<<system "Your increased muscle mass limits flexibility. Backward and lateral reach is reduced compared to a less muscular build. This body prioritizes force generation over range of motion. Overhead work and reaching behind your back may require adjustment.">>

<<system "Arm strength. Your grip strength exceeds 60 kilograms of force. Your maximum pressing force exceeds your body weight. Demonstrate: lift the composite chair with your right hand.">>

The chair from Module 4 had not fully receded into the floor   it sat at the edge of the seating area, its composite frame gleaming in the clinical light. Avan approached it. Reached down with one hand. Wrapped his fingers around the seat edge and pulled.

The chair came off the floor like it was made of paper. Not slowly   not with effort   but with a sudden, violent ease that sent it rocketing upward past his waist, past his chest, past his shoulder, his arm straightening overhead with the momentum because his muscles had applied to a 4-kilogram chair the force calibrated for a 40-kilogram expectation.

The chair flew from his grip. Launched from his open fingers like a launched projectile, spinning end over end across the apartment. It struck the far wall with a crack that split the air   composite shattering against matte charcoal, fragments scattering across the chrome floor, the neon veins in the impact zone flaring white with the shock. A crack spiderwebbed through the wall panel. The fragments skittered and spun, settling in a debris field of broken furniture.

Silence.

Avan stared at his hand. Open. Empty. The fingers that had held the chair trembling   not with effort but with the aftershock of understanding what they'd done. His breath came in one long, uneven pull. His eyes were wide.

<<avan "I   I didn't   I just LIFTED it ">>

<<system "You applied approximately 35 kilograms of lifting force to a 4-kilogram object. The disparity between intended and actual force output caused the object to become a projectile. This is the central risk of your avatar's upper body: the force your muscles generate vastly exceeds what your cognitive model expects.">>

The broken chair lay in pieces against the far wall. A chrome fragment caught the light and threw a glint across the ceiling. In the mirror, Avan's reflection showed a man with one arm still raised, palm open, staring at the wreckage he'd created by trying to pick something up.

<<system "Every physical interaction must be recalibrated. Grasping objects. Turning handles. Shaking hands. Touching people. Your default force level is sufficient to fracture bone, deform metal, and cause severe injury. You must learn to modulate consciously.">>

<<avan "Touching… people.">>

His voice was hollow. He looked at his hands   both of them now, turning them over, the massive palms and long fingers and thick tendons that moved beneath the skin with hydraulic precision. Then he looked at me. At my arms, thin and bare. At my shoulders, narrow and soft. At the body standing three meters away that weighed 56 kilograms less than his, that had half the bone density and a quarter of the muscle mass.

He could break me. Without trying. Without meaning to. A grip too tight on my wrist. A pull too sharp on my arm. A reflexive grab during a startled moment. The math was brutal and the system had just demonstrated it in composite shrapnel.

<<system "Grip calibration exercise. Approach User Leona Hart. Take her right hand. Apply minimal pressure. The system will measure force output.">>

Avan didn't move. His fists clenched at his sides   then opened deliberately, fingers spreading, the conscious act of a person who had just watched their hand throw a chair through a wall choosing to make themselves open.

He walked toward me. Slow. Each step controlled. His eyes on my face, not my body   holding my gaze the way someone holds a lifeline.

He stopped at arm's reach. His right hand lifted. Hovered. The fingers were shaking   fine tremors, barely visible, the vibration of enormous force being consciously, desperately restrained.

<<avan "I'm scared I'll hurt you.">>

Ava's words. Ava's fear. Delivered in a voice that could shake walls.

I reached up and took his hand.

My fingers settled against his palm   thin, short, pale against bronze   and his hand closed around them. Gently. So gently. The pressure was feather-light, his fingers curling with an exaggerated slowness, every ounce of force metered and monitored and terrified.

<<system "Force reading: 2.3 kilograms. Within safe parameters. User Leona Hart, confirm comfort level.">>

<<leona "It's okay, Ava. That's   that's perfect. You're not hurting me.">>

His grip tightened fractionally. 2.3 became 2.8. Still gentle. Still safe. But I could feel the potential coiled behind it   the dormant power in those fingers, held in check by will alone. His hand could crush mine. Could fold it like wet paper and instead it cradled it, trembling, wrapped around my fingers with a tenderness so desperate it ached.

<<system "Force reading stable. User Avan Morgan demonstrates conscious modulation. This calibration must be maintained for all interpersonal contact.">>

He didn't let go. The system didn't tell him to. The mirrors showed a large man holding a small woman's hand with the delicacy of someone handling a bird, and the neon veins in the walls wove their heartbeats together   his slow and deep, mine fast and light   in a pattern that pulsed softer than any reading the apartment had displayed since the guide began.

<<system "This concludes Module 5: Upper Body Familiarization. Both users have been introduced to the primary parameters of their avatar's upper body structure, strength, and sensitivity.">>

The overlays faded. The mirrors loosened their ring, sliding outward to their standard arc. The shattered chair lay against the far wall   the system making no move to repair it, as if leaving the evidence served as its own lesson.

<<system "Module 6 will begin in ninety seconds. Subject: Lower Body Familiarization. This module contains explicit anatomical content. Both users are advised to prepare.">>

Avan's hand tightened around mine. 3.1 kilograms. Still safe. Still shaking.

Neither of us spoke. The city burned outside the windows. The broken chair glittered on the floor. Somewhere beneath the fear and the strangeness and the relentless clinical light, two things sat side by side in the silence   my grief for the body that used to open jars without thinking, and his grief for the breasts he'd touched the absence of and found only armor where softness used to live.

Different losses. Same silence. Same hand, holding on.

Ninety seconds.

